  "metadata": {
    "title": "The Harp Stay",
    "description": "A cable-stayed bridge over a river, wide enough for the hay wagon. A single H-shaped tower stands in midstream, and straight stays run down from it to hold up the deck: no arches, no piers at the banks. The stays on each side run parallel, like the strings of a harp, which is what engineers call this layout. 37 bricks.\n\n## How it is built\n\nEach step is a group in the Editor, so you can select it, delete it or build it again yourself.\n\n1. **River**: four blue Slab 4x4s make a river 8 wide.\n2. **Tower**: two legs in midstream, one on each side of the road, each two Pillars stacked.\n3. **Crossbeam**: a Beam turned 90° (press **R**) across the tops of the legs, high over the road.\n4. **Stays**: on each side of the road and each side of the tower, three Diagonal Braces. Two end to end make a long stay from near the top of the tower to the deck, and one below it makes a short stay parallel to it. The braces on the east side are turned 180° so they slope down away from the tower.\n5. **Deck**: six wooden Plate 2x4s side by side, 12 long and 4 wide, hanging from the stays.\n6. **Ramps**: four Shallow Slopes on each bank lead from the ground up to the deck. On the east side they are turned 180° so they climb toward the bridge.\n7. **Lanterns**: one on top of each tower leg. In World View they light up at night.\n\n## Wide enough for the hay wagon\n\nThe hay wagon is about 2 long and 1.4 wide over its wheels, and it takes up a circle 1.6 across. The deck is 4 wide, and the tower's legs stand outside it, so the whole width is road, with 1.2 to spare on each side. The crossbeam is nearly 5 above the deck, so the hay can be piled as high as it will go.\n\nThe top of each ramp is exactly level with the deck, so a wagon rolls on without catching an edge. Over the river the stays run along both edges of the deck, so they double as rails and a wagon can't drive off into the water.\n\n## Bricks\n\n- River: 4 Slab 4x4\n- Tower: 4 Pillar\n- Crossbeam: 1 Beam\n- Stays: 12 Diagonal Brace 2x2\n- Deck: 6 Plate 2x4\n- Ramps: 8 Shallow Slope 2x1\n- Lanterns: 2 Lantern\n\n37 bricks in all.",
